  "live_records": {
    "q-335195": {
      "dom_id": "step-q335195",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "$$\n{x}^{′}=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{aligned}]x+[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the system of ODEs above. The equilibrium point of the system is $[1,\\,2]^{T}.$ Which of the following is the system obtained by shifting the equilibrium to the origin?",
      "worked_solution": "To shift the system's equilibrium from ${x}^{∗}$ to the origin, we define the deviation vector\n\n$$\nu=x-{x}^{∗}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\nu=x-[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\,⇒\\,x=u+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\,\\text{and}\\,{x}^{′}={u}^{′}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x$ and ${x}^{′}$ into the given system, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′} & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{aligned}]x+[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {u}^{′} & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{aligned}](u+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}])+[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{aligned}]u+[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{aligned}]u+[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{aligned}]u.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the shifted system is\n\n$$\n{u}^{′}=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{aligned}]u.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
