    "q-335520": {
      "dom_id": "step-q335520",
      "name": "Question 12",
      "problem": "A nonlinear system of ODEs has exactly three equilibrium points.  The system is then shifted using the transformation $u=x-{x}^{∗},$ where ${x}^{∗}$ is one of the equilibria. Which of the following statements about the number of equilibria in the shifted system is guaranteed to be true?",
      "worked_solution": "A shift of coordinates is a translation of the phase space and does not alter the structure of the system’s equilibrium set. Each equilibrium point of the original system is translated to a corresponding equilibrium in the shifted coordinates.\n\nThus, although one of the equilibria is moved to the origin, the total number of equilibrium points remains the same.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"The shifted system still has exactly three equilibrium points.\"",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
